# why-escalated.rq — the chain of judgements for one region, in the order they were made,
# each with its rationale and (where the candidate was refuted) the observation that killed
# it. Answers spec 2026-08-07 §4 question 1: "why was this region escalated?"
#
# ?supersededBy is bound when a LATER reading of this band replaced this one (section repair
# adopts a pass-2 re-read and links the two verdict decisions with dec:supersedes). It binds
# at REGION level, so every row of a superseded chain carries it — a consumer reading any one
# row learns the whole chain was replaced. Follow effective-chain.rq for the live reading.
PREFIX dec: <https://w3id.org/iladub/dec#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?order ?judgement ?chosen ?rationale ?supersededBy WHERE {
  ?d a dec:DecisionHolon ; dec:regarding ?region ; dec:order ?order ;
     rdfs:label ?judgement ; dec:rationale ?rationale .
  OPTIONAL { ?d dec:chosen/rdfs:label ?chosen }
# ?supersededBy IS THE HEAD OF THE CHAIN, NOT THE NEXT LINK (2026-09-14, R225 D2). The
# OPTIONAL below joins ?v1 — every decision regarding ?region — to the decisions that supersede
# it TRANSITIVELY, and keeps only the one nothing supersedes. Binding the IMMEDIATE superseder
# was correct only while a band could be superseded once: under D2 a band can be section-
# repaired AND adopted over, so the immediate superseder is itself replaced, and a consumer
# following it would be sent to a stale middle link — the same defect effective-chain.rq's
# header describes from the other side.
#
# THE MULTIPLICATION THIS BLOCK USED TO WARN ABOUT IS NOW PREVENTED UPSTREAM, which is why the
# cross-product is no longer the hazard it was. A second incoming dec:supersedes edge on one
# verdict is refused by dec:SupersededOnceShape, and document.py's adoption site chains rather
# than fanning in (`_effective_verdict`). A chain has exactly one head, so this yields one
# ?supersededBy per superseded ?v1 rather than one per (?v1, ?v2) pair.
  OPTIONAL {
    ?v1 dec:regarding ?region .
    ?supersededBy dec:supersedes+ ?v1 .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?later dec:supersedes ?supersededBy }
  }
}
ORDER BY ?order
